  "notes": "{留|と}める means to fasten or secure something in place using a pin, clip, screw, or similar fastener.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: Xを〜で{留|と}める (fasten X with ~)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ピンで{留|と}める: to pin\n- クリップで{留|と}める: to clip\n- ねじで{留|と}める: to screw in\n- {髪|かみ}を{留|と}める: to pin up hair\n- ボタンを{留|と}める: to fasten a button\n\nHOMOPHONES (IMPORTANT):\nAll read とめる but written with different kanji:\n- {止|と}める: to stop (movement, action)\n- {泊|と}める: to let someone stay overnight\n- {留|と}める: to fasten, to pin (this entry)\n\nThe kanji is the key to distinguishing these in writing.",
